# Mobile app environment — copy to .env for local overrides.
#
# Only EXPO_PUBLIC_* variables are bundled into the app (via Metro at
# dev-server time, and via eas build `env`/EAS environment variables at
# build time). None of these are secrets: they ship inside the APK by
# design. Real secrets must never live here.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# API base URL (REQUIRED for standalone/release builds)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Full base URL of the API, INCLUDING the `/api/v1` prefix.
#
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.20:3001/api/v1
#
# - Development (expo start / Expo Go / dev builds): optional. The app
#   derives the API host from the Metro dev-server host automatically, so a
#   physical phone on the same WiFi just works; the Android emulator falls
#   back to 10.0.2.2 and the iOS simulator/web to localhost (overridable via
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_PORT).
# - Standalone builds (EAS preview/production): MANDATORY. A release build
#   without this variable shows a configuration error on the sign-in screen
#   instead of silently targeting the phone's own localhost — there is no
#   fallback by design. The value must be a URL the device can actually
#   reach (never localhost/127.0.0.1).
# - Against an API running with NODE_ENV=production the URL must be HTTPS:
#   the API issues its refresh cookie with Secure; SameSite=None, which no
#   device cookie jar will send over plain http — sessions cannot restore.
#EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=

# API port used for the Metro-host derivation and the dev emulator/simulator
# defaults above. Rarely needed.
#EXPO_PUBLIC_API_PORT=3001

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Maps API key for Android (react-native-maps)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Injected into the generated AndroidManifest.xml by app.config.js. The key
# travels in plaintext inside the APK (that is how the Maps SDK works); it
# is NOT a secret — but restrict it in Google Cloud to the "Maps SDK for
# Android" API plus this app's package name and signing-certificate SHA-1
# so a copied key is useless elsewhere.
#
# Leave unset for Expo Go (Maps runs on Expo's own key there). Required for
# a standalone APK/AAB that displays the live tracking map.
#EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
